2174	    /// changes to the daemon (todo #142). The status half of the lifecycle: the
2175	    /// plugin is the only code that can read a pane's buffer, so it captures the
2176	    /// viewport, runs that type's compiled patterns locally, and reports just
2177	    /// the derived one-word state (never the output) - and only on a *change*,
2178	    /// so a steady agent costs no subprocess. Gated to the Todos gatekeeper so
